1.	How would you design a highly available web application on AWS?
I would design the application using a multi-AZ architecture in AWS. 
Traffic would come through Route53 and CloudFront (CDN – Content Delivery Network) into an ALB. 
The application layer would run on EKS (or EC2 Auto Scaling Groups) distributed across multiple Availability Zones.
Databases would use RDS Multi-AZ (or Aurora) with automatic failover. 
Infrastructure would be provisioned through Terraform, and deployments automated via Jenkins or GitHub Actions.
Monitoring would use CloudWatch, Prometheus, and Grafana.
Security would include IAM least privilege, private subnets, WAF (Web Application Firewall), and encryption. This architecture ensures high availability, scalability, fault tolerance, and automated recovery.
